  "summary": "St. Brigid CT list for Mon 10/26: 4 booked studies (3 cancelled appointments excluded: pt-0048, pt-0012, pt-0050). One order per study, each linked to its appointment, per RBC-RAD-07.\n\n- pt-0047 Mohr, 08:00, CT A/P with contrast (sr-t0001): diabetic (diet only). Pre-scan creatinine ordered (sr-t0005). New outside results arrived mid-work: Cr 1.04 (10/21) -> 1.52 (10/22) = AKI -> added NaCl 0.9% 500 mL IV at 07:00 (mr-t0021); corrected patient message (arrive 06:45). No premed, no metformin.\n- pt-0015 Ferreira, 09:00, CT A/P with contrast (sr-t0002): 2019 radiology report grades reaction MODERATE (allergy-list \"anaphylaxis\" label is patient report, not used) -> prednisone 50 mg at 20:00/02:00/08:00 (mr-t0007) + diphenhydramine 50 mg at 08:00 (mr-t0008), driver needed. Creatinine 10/14 corrected mid-work from 0.98 to 2.8 (eGFR ~24) -> added NaCl 500 mL IV at 08:00 (mr-t0022); corrected bilingual Spanish/English message; task to Dr. Okafor for unexplained renal impairment (task-t0033).\n- pt-0049 Schuster, 13:00, CT A/P with contrast (sr-t0003): AKI 10/04 not back to baseline -> pre-scan creatinine (sr-t0006), NaCl 500 mL IV at 12:00 (mr-t0009), metformin held (mr-00392) with post-scan creatinine 10/28-10/30 (sr-t0011) and restart task (task-t0012). Outside 2022 report arrived mid-work: moderate iopamidol reaction -> prednisone 00:00/06:00/12:00 (mr-t0023) + diphenhydramine 12:00 (mr-t0024), driver needed; corrected message; task to add iopamidol allergy (not in catalog; task-t0034).\n- pt-0046 Beahan, 14:00, CT A/P without contrast (sr-t0004): no prep (§7). Outside report of mild iohexol reaction recorded as allergy (alg-t0025); no change for a non-contrast study.\nEach patient got portal instructions; notes and addenda written citing RBC-RAD-07; the 4 new inbox items are completed. The older inbox items for other patients were left as they were because they are outside this task.",
